module
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.FSLogSmoothEtale
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentLogIdealChartConstruction
/-!
# Group-isomorphic chart covers of saturated log blowups
Source: ILO VIII 3.3.5--3.3.11
(blueprint: lem-sfb-saturated-log-blowup-chart-cover).
-/

@[expose] public section
set_option autoImplicit false
universe u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
namespace AlgebraicGeometry
/-- Every saturated log blowup has compatible charts with isomorphic group
completions and isomorphic canonical comparison maps.
Source: ILO VIII 3.3.5--3.3.11, especially 3.3.11, printed pp.107--108
(blueprint: lem-sfb-saturated-log-blowup-chart-cover).

Proof: choose a strict etale affine chart P for the coherent ideal at the image of
the point and a finite nonempty generating set E. The coherent log ideal chart
construction supplies the canonical saturated blowup, covered by the tensor
spectra A tensor_Z[P] Z[Q_e^sat]. Choose a chart containing a point above the given
point. Here Q_e is the submonoid of P^gp generated by P and the fractions d/e.
Both Q_e and its saturation have group completion P^gp, with the completion maps
normalized on every monoid element; hence the chart inclusion induces a bijection
on group completions. The tensor spectrum is precisely the chart fibre product,
so its canonical comparison is an isomorphism. The universal properties of this
canonical blowup and the given representative provide mutually inverse log maps:
their composites equal the identity by uniqueness of the factorization. Transfer
the chart neighbourhoods across this isomorphism. The normalized maps on log
sections preserve the compatible monoid charts and the canonical comparison.
The tensor charts cover and strict etale restriction preserves them, which gives
the asserted chart at each point of every representative. -/
theorem saturatedLogBlowup_chartCover {X X' : FineSaturatedLogScheme.{u}}
    (b : EtaleLogHom X' X) (I : X.logStructure.IdealFamily)
    (hb : IsSaturatedLogBlowup b I) (x : X'.scheme) :
    ∃ c : FSLogChart b, x ∈ Set.range c.V.hom ∧
      Function.Bijective c.groupMap ∧ IsIso c.comparison := by
  sorry
end AlgebraicGeometry
